_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 67
---
order: 67
---
short_label: X.67
---
statement: A straight line commensurable with a bimedial straight line is itself also bimedial and the same in order.
---
proof:

Let *AB* be bimedial, and let *CD* be commensurable in length with *AB*.

I say that *CD* is bimedial and the same in order with *AB*.

Since *AB* is bimedial, divide it into its medials at *E*.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="250" height="95" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="X.67 diagram" src="propX67.gif"/></noscript>
